# Composable Conventions (reference: https://github.com/vueuse/vueuse)

Treat VueUse as the style authority. When unsure, find the closest `@vueuse/core`
function and copy its shape.

## Signature

Primary inputs are positional; everything optional goes in a trailing options object.
Never bundle required inputs into the options bag.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — required data hidden in an options bag
export function useAutoSave<T>(options: { source: MaybeRefOrGetter<T>; save: SaveFn; debounceMs?: number })

// ✅ GOOD
export function useAutoSave<T>(
  source: MaybeRefOrGetter<T>,
  save: SaveFn<T>,
  options: UseAutoSaveOptions = {},
): UseAutoSaveReturn
```

## Types

Export `UseXxxOptions` / `UseXxxReturn` interfaces and annotate the return type
explicitly. Options extend `ConfigurableWindow` when the composable touches
browser globals.

## Return shape

Single value → return the ref itself. Multiple values → return an object.
Tuples are reserved for the `useToggle` pattern (value + setter).

```ts
// ❌ BAD
return [code, authorize];
// ✅ GOOD
return { code, authorize };
```

## Reactivity

- Accept `MaybeRefOrGetter<T>`, unwrap with `toValue()`. Never `unref()`.
- `shallowRef` by default; `ref`/`deep` only when nested tracking is required.

## Lifecycle & side effects

- Use `tryOnScopeDispose` / `tryOnMounted`, not bare `onScopeDispose` / `onMounted`,
  so the composable stays callable outside a component scope.
- Every listener/timer registered must be cleaned up. Prefer `useEventListener`,
  `useTimeoutFn`, `useIntervalFn` over hand-rolled equivalents.
- Modules must have **no import-time side effects**. Export a function; let callers invoke it.

## Browser globals & config

Read nothing from `window`, `document`, `location`, `navigator`, or
`import.meta.env` directly. Take `{ window = defaultWindow }` from options, guard
with `isClient`, and surface app config (AppId, feature flags, paths) as options
with env-backed defaults.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const appId = import.meta.env.VITE_WECHAT_APPID ?? '';
// ✅ GOOD
const { appId = import.meta.env.VITE_WECHAT_APPID ?? '' } = options;
```

## Naming

`useXxx` camelCase functions. File names stay **kebab-case** per `AGENTS.md`
(`use-auto-save/use-auto-save.ts`) — this is the one place we intentionally
diverge from VueUse's `useAutoSave/index.ts` layout.

JSDoc in English, with an `@example` block showing the call site.
